{
  "area": "honduras-roatan",
  "method": "Roatán (whole island, West Bay Point to Camp Bay and Port Royal, north and south shores) plus the offshore seamounts and Cayos Cochinos dived from Roatán. Official list: the Roatán Marine Park mooring dataset ('RMP dive sites', folder 'September 2026 dive sites.xlsx', 435 rows with lat/lon, depth and maintenance status; the Google My Maps layer Roatan Divers embeds as the Roatan Marine Park Dive Site Map, read as KML), counted as one list; its snorkel-site and yacht-mooring rows were ignored, and positions are its own, rounded to 5 decimals. Its rows mostly carry sponsor names, so a traditional operator name was matched to a mooring only on the same name in the same area. Operator lists, one each: CoCo View Resort's site page; Roatan Dive Center's north-shore, south-shore and wreck pages; Roatan Splash Inn's site log; Roatan Divers' best-dive-sites article; Coconut Tree Divers' site page (domain no longer resolves, read from its May 2026 Wayback copy); Anthony's Key Resort's site page and its public daily dive-sites log (Google Calendar, entries from 2025-01-01 on, spelling variants merged); Native Sons' fun-dive page; Sun Divers' top-ten, beginner-site and wreck pages; Turquoise Divers' site page; Blue Reef Explorers' site page. West End Divers' site list (westenddivers.info) is a parked domain and was not used; DivePlanner Pro's per-shop 'reachable' lists and magazine or aggregator guides were leads only. A site is counted when it is named on at least two of these independent lists and is a recreational scuba dive; a dive sold as one over several moorings is one row with aliases. Excluded: one-list names (grouped per operator where several), the Josie J (213 ft, technical only) and Cordelia Banks (closed to divers). Cayos Cochinos itself has no operator site list beyond Blue Reef Explorers and the Fundación Cayos Cochinos publishes none, so only the seamounts reach two lists. Counted 2026-10-14.",
